{"type":"user","uuid":"c93f3b23-d850-4585-95a2-18478f08d930","session_id":"d4e8b5fa-8941-49ea-95d0-ca3a56207d4f","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_14497639d87b4770b4acd698","is_error":false,"content":"Read lines 281-305 of 448 from app/src/main/java/swati4star/createpdf/activity/MainActivity.java"}]}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"05ef7e70-f069-4b75-9193-12922bda5a5e","session_id":"d4e8b5fa-8941-49ea-95d0-ca3a56207d4f","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"05ef7e70-f069-4b75-9193-12922bda5a5e","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All the changes are in place. Let me summarize the fix:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nThe bug was in `MainActivity.java` — the `onBackPressed()` method immediately navigated to `HomeFragment` when the user was on any non-home fragment, without checking if a file picker dialog was currently displayed.\n\n### Root Cause\nWhen a user clicks the \"Select File\" button (MorphingButton) on fragments like `InvertPdfFragment`, `RemovePagesFragment`, etc., a file picker activity is launched via `startActivityForResult()`. This activity appears on top of MainActivity. When the user presses back to dismiss the picker, `MainActivity.onBackPressed()` was executing and navigating to `HomeFragment` instead of letting the picker dismiss naturally.\n\n### Fix Applied\nThree changes to `MainActivity.java`:\n\n1. **Added a boolean flag** `mFilePickerDisplayed` (line 74) to track when a file picker is displayed.\n\n\n2. **Overrode `startActivity(Intent)`** to detect file chooser intents and set the flag accordingly. Since file picker intents are wrapped by `Intent.createChooser()` with `ACTION_CHOOSER` or directly use `ACTION_GET_CONTENT`, the method checks for these actions and sets `mFilePickerDisplayed` to `true` before delegating to the superclass.\n3. **Added a check in `onBackPressed()`** that prevents navigation to HomeFragment when the file picker flag is active, allowing the picker to dismiss first.\n\nThe implementation has been verified to compile successfully.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"c5178051-55b9-45b2-b550-000f3cbc72f0","session_id":"d4e8b5fa-8941-49ea-95d0-ca3a56207d4f","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"c5178051-55b9-45b2-b550-000f3cbc72f0","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is complete and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of the changes made:\n\n## Fix Summary\n\n**File modified:** `app/src/main/java/swati4star/createpdf/activity/MainActivity.java`\n\n**Root Cause:** When a file picker is displayed (launched via `startActivityForResult()` from fragments like `InvertPdfFragment`, `RemovePagesFragment`, etc.), pressing back caused `MainActivity.onBackPressed()` to immediately navigate to `HomeFragment` instead of dismissing the file picker first.\n\n**Three changes applied:**\n\n1. **Added `mFilePickerDisplayed` flag** (line 74) — tracks when a file chooser is currently displayed\n\n2. **Added `startActivity(Intent)` override** (lines 214-225) — sets the flag when a file chooser is launched. Detects `ACTION_CHOOSER` (from `Intent.createChooser()` wrapping) and `ACTION_GET_CONTENT` (from `TextToPdfFragment`)\n\n3. **Added `onResume()` override** (lines 206-212) — clears the flag when control returns to MainActivity (covers both file selection completion and cancellation)\n\n4. **Modified `onBackPressed()`** (lines 291-295) — if `mFilePickerDisplayed` is `true`, delegates to `super.onBackPressed()` to let the system dismiss the picker first, then returns without navigating to HomeFragment\n\n**Behavior:**\n- User clicks file selector → flag set to `true` → file picker appears\n- User presses back → flag is `true` → `super.onBackPressed()` dismisses the picker → user stays on the same fragment\n- User selects a file or cancels picker → `onResume()` clears flag → normal navigation resumes"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":61369,"output_tokens":687,"cache_read_input_tokens":60192,"total_tokens":62056}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"65d1bedc-ce5c-46aa-a5e7-4083a2bf331f","session_id":"d4e8b5fa-8941-49ea-95d0-ca3a56207d4f","is_error":false,"duration_ms":342940,"duration_api_ms":237570,"num_turns":5,"result":"The fix is complete and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of the changes made:\n\n## Fix Summary\n\n**File modified:** `app/src/main/java/swati4star/createpdf/activity/MainActivity.java`\n\n**Root Cause:** When a file picker is displayed (launched via `startActivityForResult()` from fragments like `InvertPdfFragment`, `RemovePagesFragment`, etc.), pressing back caused `MainActivity.onBackPressed()` to immediately navigate to `HomeFragment` instead of dismissing the file picker first.\n\n**Three changes applied:**\n\n1. **Added `mFilePickerDisplayed` flag** (line 74) — tracks when a file chooser is currently displayed\n\n2. **Added `startActivity(Intent)` override** (lines 214-225) — sets the flag when a file chooser is launched. Detects `ACTION_CHOOSER` (from `Intent.createChooser()` wrapping) and `ACTION_GET_CONTENT` (from `TextToPdfFragment`)\n\n3. **Added `onResume()` override** (lines 206-212) — clears the flag when control returns to MainActivity (covers both file selection completion and cancellation)\n\n4. **Modified `onBackPressed()`** (lines 291-295) — if `mFilePickerDisplayed` is `true`, delegates to `super.onBackPressed()` to let the system dismiss the picker first, then returns without navigating to HomeFragment\n\n**Behavior:**\n- User clicks file selector → flag set to `true` → file picker appears\n- User presses back → flag is `true` → `super.onBackPressed()` dismisses the picker → user stays on the same fragment\n- User selects a file or cancels picker → `onResume()` clears flag → normal navigation resumes","usage":{"input_tokens":1524390,"output_tokens":19237,"cache_read_input_tokens":1326336,"total_tokens":1543627},"permission_denials":[]}
